Found by a coordinator feature-gap review, 2026-08-30. Verified on master
@ 91a296c. Pre-existing.

## Defect
The server advertises an execute-command:

    src/server/mod.rs:1043-1046
    execute_command_provider: Some(ExecuteCommandOptions {
        commands: vec!["openplanet.regenerateTypeDb".into()],
        ..Default::default()
    }),

No client ever invokes it. Verified in the extension repo
(../lsp-openplanet-ext/packages/vscode-ext): the only two `executeCommand`
calls in `src/extension.ts` are at :60 and :142, and BOTH are
`workbench.action.openSettings` for the `openplanetLsp.serverPath` warning
paths. Neither touches `regenerateTypeDb`.

`contributes.commands` in the extension's package.json contains exactly one
entry, `openplanetLsp.restart` ("Restart Server"), so there is also no
command-palette route a user could take manually.

Net: a working server capability that nothing can reach.

## Impact
Regenerating the type DB is exactly the recovery action a user needs after
updating Openplanet or the game — the case where the LSP's symbol surface goes
stale and every diagnostic becomes suspect. Today the only route is the CLI
(`openplanet-lsp typedb ...`), which a VS Code user has no reason to know
about.

## Work
- Contribute `openplanetLsp.regenerateTypeDb` ("Openplanet LSP: Regenerate
  Type Database") in the extension's `contributes.commands`, wired to
  `client.sendRequest(ExecuteCommandRequest.type, ...)` for
  `openplanet.regenerateTypeDb`.
- Report progress and outcome to the user — this is a long operation. Use a
  progress notification, and on completion report what changed (versions
  before/after) rather than a bare "done".
- Verify the SERVER side actually implements the handler and does something.
  Check `execute_command` exists on the LanguageServer impl; if the command is
  advertised but unimplemented, that is the real bug and this ticket covers
  implementing it or removing the advertisement. DO NOT assume it works
  because it is listed — an advertised-but-unimplemented command is exactly
  the failure this ticket exists to find.
- While there, audit for the inverse: any command the extension sends that the
  server does not advertise.

## Design decision (coordinator, 2026-08-30)
If the handler turns out to be missing, IMPLEMENT it rather than dropping the
advertisement — the capability is genuinely wanted (see Impact). Removing the
advertisement is only correct if regeneration is unsafe to trigger from the
editor, which should be argued explicitly, not assumed.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)
Server side:
- `execute_command_advertised_commands_are_all_implemented`: every string in
  `ExecuteCommandOptions.commands` is dispatched by the `execute_command`
  handler. Generalize it — this must fail for ANY future advertised-but-
  unimplemented command, not just this one.
- an unknown command name -> proper JSON-RPC error, not a panic.

Extension side (vitest, existing harness at ../lsp-openplanet-ext):
- the command is registered on activation
- invoking it sends the right `workspace/executeCommand` request
- server failure surfaces an error notification rather than failing silently
- the command is present in `contributes.commands` (guards the palette route,
  which is separate from registration)

